    {
      "id": "claim_df6eede5d9044a15b4f3412e98b51519",
      "statement": "Known hardware design bug (found 2026-09): relay driver transistors Q1/Q2 on connector J7 are populated as IRLML2244 P-channel high-side FETs that assert +12V on the relay-coil pins, but the EBL expects a low-side pull-to-GND signal; as a result the relay never switches regardless of pulse length or sense-pin state. Proposed, not-yet-verified fix is to replace Q1/Q2 with IRLML6244 N-channel FETs (same SOT-23 footprint).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/CLAUDE.md#L18-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fdc96ac58cf9e4f026fddad7128de2cf26cc2db8e641e6a665ad75b534037ebd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/README.md#L108-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dabff0eafa8fcf345e6a1db1fcc8b4fc6256a006e8d62f3a800c6ee037365ec3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/memory-bank/progress.md#L41-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:695ee2ab2569eb6f81cea567534ff9e8a40320b10bf690a4949d07711dd7eec6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5479ee06255e49efa745f1b779aa37a3",
      "statement": "A separate, more severe physical-damage incident on 2026-08-30 (reversed-polarity mating of connector J7) hard-shorted the GPIO13 (multimedia) output stage and exposed GPIO17 (light) to a swapped 12V control signal; GPIO18 (pump) was unaffected. The 12V house-battery control lines GPIO11/GPIO12 are also routed through J7 and are suspected, but not yet conclusively verified, to be damaged from the same incident, making this specific physical board unusable for normal operation pending a new PCB revision, independent of the Q1/Q2 design bug.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/sensor_config.h#L237-L245",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a4a9908484da4f141075a7e30513061de08e9c2089fe4671ccdf020063bb995d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/memory-bank/progress.md#L52-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b8b06bf65f6ff73264b6efb71448b3db0f801da56c800f5c23eacbed6dc8faa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4d379623df25443d8268a7951d049ca5",
      "statement": "A previously fixed firmware defect (2026-08-30) caused GPIO11/GPIO12 (and GPIO17 during debugging) to remain frozen at their pre-sleep level after every touch wakeup because gpio_hold_dis() was missing for these pins in app_main.c; the fix makes gpio_hold_dis(GPIO11)/gpio_hold_dis(GPIO12) unconditional at the start of app_main(), before any later gpio_set_level() calls take effect.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/app_main.c#L138-L150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a322a19e38fea37812e926b978f909b42491bd6c56d2b1010a6a1827075e03d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/memory-bank/progress.md#L51-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b426996ef42d60bcd9a8c1ae35ee0e7f10102d2a0cc11b60ea81a8e0963a5312:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0ab8ea727ea1462cb44d73a48a367940",
      "statement": "deep_sleep_enter_cold() freezes GPIO11/GPIO12 LOW without issuing any relay pulse (unlike deep_sleep_enter(), which pulses GPIO12 before sleeping), because the bistable relay's actual state is unknown/unchanged at that boot-time code path and an unintended pulse must be avoided.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/hal/deep_sleep.c#L105-L123",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c66cc49a3bacd7040dc0d0d0f4d81f87cd9d68331062dc3f5bdddf72e180a973:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1025846e6636431c974286e16c674888",
      "statement": "There is no automatic under-voltage protection for the 12V house-battery circuit: the sensorboard only switches the relay on explicit display command (pwr_12v_on/off), and a software-based low-voltage disconnect comparable to an EBL Batteriewächter cutoff is an open, unimplemented feature.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/memory-bank/progress.md#L39-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36bbfb907ca0281144dadb626acb93c95f96c61ce51115b2bbe5493f0b1bedb7:"
        }
      ]
    }
